# Whiteboard photographs.
#
# These are the primary source for the feed board design (issue #2) and the
# richest domain evidence we have, but they are large binaries and they show
# volunteers' names and personal phone numbers. Kept on disk, out of git.
fhhr-whiteboard/

# Build output and dependencies
node_modules/
.output/
.nitro/
.tanstack/
dist/

# Local configuration. Secrets never enter the repository; .env.example is the
# list of what a machine needs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The VPS template is the exception, and it is not one: it holds `op://`
# references rather than values, and it is in the repository because ADR 0006
# makes 1Password the source of truth and this file the record of which
# variables come from it. `render-env.sh` turns it into a real `.env` on the
# box, and that file is covered by the rule above like any other.
!deploy/.env.tpl

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
